{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"2aa452282162e92ab5eebb10970b38509d267bf398a25b409915de68e2a33081","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar doctor command / lock diagnostics","key_entities":["rebar doctor","rebar._commands.doctor_locks.py","rebar._commands.doctor.py",".ticket-write.lock",".ticket-write.lock.d",".rebar/hlc.lock",".rebar/enrich-drain.lock","rebar._store.lock.write_lock_is_busy","rebar._store.lock_owner._parse_v2_stamp","rebar._store.lock_owner._describe_stamped_pid","rebar._store.lock_owner._mkdir_lock_age_s","rebar._store.lock_owner._mkdir_lock_is_stale","doctor.schema.json","docs/cli-reference.md"],"problem_keywords":["lock health","diagnostics","observability","held lock","stale lock","lock holder liveness","lock age"],"propositions":["Operator has no diagnostic surface to inspect lock holders or determine whether held processes are alive when a store write lock is held; doctor command reports only blocking links, not lock state.","The four lock legs (tickets-write fcntl, tickets-write mkdir, hlc fcntl, enrich-drain O_EXCL) must be reported with held/free/absent state and holder identity, liveness, and hold age via the existing stamp decode and liveness primitives.","A stale lock (dead or recycled pid holder) must be identified only via the existing lock_owner._mkdir_lock_is_stale function; no independent staleness heuristic is added.","Doctor must remain read-only: lock state is never mutated, modified, or reclaimed, and --repair does not touch locks."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787430927757066001,"uuid":"97855ed8-9f6a-4369-a796-a9